-## UI: phosh
-
-`phosh` is the default UI ("complete GUI"). Rationale:
-
-- The display is a 1200x1920 portrait tablet panel; phosh's scalable mobile
-  shell fits it, and phosh already has a Duranium integration subpackage
-  (`postmarketos-ui-phosh-duranium`, pulls `phosh-os-updater`), so OS updates
-  are wired into the GUI out of the box.
-- GPU is Mali-G72 with no Panfrost yet, so rendering is software. phoc is set
-  to the pixman renderer (`WLR_RENDERER=pixman`, via the device package) which
-  is far lighter on four Cortex-A55 cores than llvmpipe, and phosh is lighter
-  than Plasma Mobile under software rendering.
-- `plasma-mobile` resolves too (`UI=plasma-mobile contrib/.../build-image.sh`)
-  if wanted; it is heavier without GPU acceleration.
+- `scripts/mkosi-container`: `MKOSI_CONTAINER_ARGS` for extra podman
+  arguments (bind mounts, `--security-opt label=disable` on SELinux hosts).
+- `contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/`: `pkgbuilder.Containerfile`,
+  `build-apks.sh`, `build-image.sh`, `install-to-userdata.sh`, `kernel/`
+  (config fragments + generator), `firmware/` and this README.
+
+## Kernel config
+
+`kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh` = `build/bringup/.config` (the live-tested
+bring-up config) + `pmos-deps.config` + `pmos-fragment.config` (pmbootstrap
+kconfigcheck categories of the APKBUILD) + `gtactive3wifi.config` (device
+fragment: no built-in initramfs, EFI stub without ZBOOT, systemd
+requirements, dm-verity/erofs/dm-crypt/loop built in, simpledrm, USB gadget
+with dwc3/PHY as modules, i2c-dev, /dev/mem for MMIO, watchdog, panic
+safety net, no PM/suspend), olddefconfig in the package builder container,
+then it checks that every line of the device fragment survived and runs
+pmbootstrap's kconfigcheck. Output: the aport's
+`config-postmarketos-exynos9810.aarch64`.
+
+## UI: GNOME
+
+The image uses the GNOME UI only (`UI=gnome` -> `postmarketos-ui-gnome`, which
+pulls `postmarketos-base-ui-gnome`; on Duranium its `-duranium` subpackage,
+`postmarketos-base-ui-gnome-duranium`, is installed automatically through
+`install_if` on `postmarketos-duranium`). No Phosh or Plasma images are built
+for this device.
+
+Rendering: the Mali-G72 runs under mainline panfrost (probed and executing GPU
+jobs on the device since 2026-10-21), so mutter uses Mesa's panfrost driver;
+llvmpipe remains the fallback if the GPU driver is not loaded.
 
 ## Disk layout: a GPT nested inside userdata (sda31)
 
@@ -95,19 +114,23 @@ resizing for the 52 GiB target. The installer only writes the image bytes.
