-an arm64 Alpine container (`build-apks.sh`, no pmbootstrap needed) into
-`build/wt/duranium-localpkgs`, symlinks `duranium/pmaports` to the worktree,
-and runs mkosi with that package directory. Output lands in
+`build-apks.sh` builds the packages above in an x86_64 postmarketOS
+container with `CARCH=aarch64` and the aarch64 cross compiler (like
+pmbootstrap's cross-native mode, no qemu) into `build/wt/duranium-localpkgs`;
+sources are cached in `build/wt/duranium-distfiles`. `build-image.sh`
+symlinks `duranium/pmaports` to the worktree and runs mkosi in its container
+(`scripts/mkosi-container`) with that package directory. Output:
 `mkosi.output/samsung-gtactive3wifi_phosh_edge/`.
 
+The UKI embeds exactly one DTB (`exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dtb`, the kernel
+package ships only that one), so mkosi uses an unconditional `.dtb` section
+rather than `.dtbauto`: it does not depend on U-Boot's DT compatible.
+
